<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<assembly manifestVersion="1.0" xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:asm.v1">
  <assemblyIdentity version="1.0.0.0" name="Longwave.WindowsCompanion.Backend"/>
  <trustInfo xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:asm.v2">
    <security>
      <requestedPrivileges xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:asm.v3">
        <!-- asInvoker on purpose. Mobile Hotspot configuration/start is the ONLY thing here
             that needs administrator rights, and it now elevates on demand: the hotspot panel
             re-spawns this same executable in its tethering-host role via ShellExecute "runas",
             so the consent prompt appears when the user turns tethering on and at no other
             time. See TetheringElevation.cs.

             The PCVR path must NOT be elevated, and that is not a preference: an elevated
             process has XR_RUNTIME_JSON ignored by the OpenXR loader, which forced the whole
             runtime-registration layout (the machine registry default had to be CloudXR because
             it was the only way to steer an elevated broker). Unelevated, the env var works and
             the registry default is free to belong to games. Verified on the RTX host on
             2026-07-28: NvStreamManager, CloudXrService and the session broker all run at medium
             integrity, the ipc_cloudxr pipe lands under the user's own AppData\Local\Temp, and
             the broker selected CloudXR through XR_RUNTIME_JSON.

             Note for future edits: a double hyphen cannot appear inside an XML comment, and a
             manifest that fails to parse does not warn at build time. It fails at launch with
             "side-by-side configuration is incorrect", which reads like a missing runtime.

             Harmless when launched as a service (the SCM grants the service account's token
             regardless of the manifest). -->
        <requestedExecutionLevel level="asInvoker" uiAccess="false" />
      </requestedPrivileges>
    </security>
  </trustInfo>
  <compatibility xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:compatibility.v1">
    <application>
      <supportedOS Id="{8e0f7a12-bfb3-4fe8-b9a5-48fd50a15a9a}" />
    </application>
  </compatibility>
</assembly>
